/-- `a ⌈/⌉ b ≤ k` says that `k` pieces of size `b` cover `a`. Mathlib's `ceilDiv_le_iff_le_mul` has
`b * k` on the right. -/
theorem ceilDiv_le_iff {a b k : ℕ} (hb : 0 < b) : a ⌈/⌉ b ≤ k ↔ a ≤ k * b := by
